From ed8c3cebde421b5abe86242df7c91874a22b9511 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 11:57:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 138/162] fix: the clouds' atmospheric haze replaced the sky -
 it followed the sun's convention, not the dome's

User: a hard horizontal band above the horizon; inside the volumetric-cloud volume's screen
region the sky is a flat grey-blue haze, outside it the plain sky. Present with every camera,
with volumetric fog off, and only the cloud altitude moved the edge.

Measured in the editor (r_HDRDebug 1, airfield): the Nishita dome is fine (zenith 370 cd/m2 at
17:00, follows r_SceneReferredNishitaScale, survives six convention flips), but it collapses
near sunset (17:54 -> 199, 18:12 -> 22 cd/m2) while the CE sun still lights the scene. In that
regime the visible sky is the vol-fog far plane plus the cloud pass's atmospheric Rayleigh haze,
and the haze was PI / 0.37 = 8.5x heavier relative to the dome than in stock: S2 had treated
sunIntensityForAtmospheric as a fourth PI site (left undivided on the scene-referred path to
match GetSunColor), and S8 scaled the dome by 0.37 without touching it. The term never meets
shadeColorFromSun in any expression; it is a sky-side quantity.

Fix: on the scene-referred path the haze takes the dome's convention - the stock divide by PI
stays, and it is multiplied by r_SceneReferredNishitaScale like the dome is in
CSkyLightManager. Off the switch the stock expression is evaluated unchanged. After the fix,
at 18:00 the zenith haze is 0.14x the dome (was ~10x at 18:12); at 17:00 no slab.

Kept for a later stage: deriving the haze from the dome's own Rayleigh radiance (one sky
brightness driving both models, and the haze dying with the dome at sunset), and the Nishita
collapse near the horizon itself (calibration; the airfield preset authors Kr 0.5 and 380 nm
for all three wavelengths). decisions/s9-cloud-haze.md, research/s9-cloud-haze-ratio.md,
research/s9-cloud-sky-split.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HXzRVK4yBVDUNfdWXEwV5y
---
 Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp | 28 ++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp b/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp
index cb3b500d..3b05bdab 100644
--- a/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp
+++ b/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/TimeOfDay.cpp
@@ -1356,13 +1356,27 @@ void CTimeOfDay::UpdateEnvLighting(bool forceUpdate)
 		const Vec3 volCloudScatteringMulti = Vec3(GetValue(PARAM_VOLCLOUD_MULTI_SCATTERING_ATTENUATION).x, GetValue(PARAM_VOLCLOUD_MULTI_SCATTERING_PRESERVATION).x, GetValue(PARAM_VOLCLOUD_POWDER_EFFECT).x);
 		p3DEngine->SetGlobalParameter(E3DPARAM_VOLCLOUD_SCATTERING_MULTI, volCloudScatteringMulti);
 
-		// The fourth PI site, and a forward replication rather than an undo: the clouds recompute
-		// the sun's engine value from lux and deliberately re-apply the divide so that it matches
-		// GetSunColor(). It therefore has to follow GetSunColor()'s convention exactly, or the
-		// clouds desync from the sun by PI. Ungated in stock CE; gated here.
-		const float sunIntensityOriginal = bSceneReferredUnits
-		                                   ? (sunIntensityLux / RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE)
-		                                   : (sunIntensityLux / RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE) / gf_PI; // divided by pi to match to GetSunColor(), it's also divided by pi in ConvertIlluminanceToLightColor().
+		// This value feeds ONLY the volumetric clouds' atmospheric Rayleigh haze
+		// (E3DPARAM_VOLCLOUD_WIND_ATMOSPHERIC.z -> sunIntensityForAtmospheric), the in-scatter the
+		// cloud pass adds on every ray that reaches the cloud layer and composites additively over the
+		// sky. It was treated as a fourth PI site (un-divided on the scene-referred path to match
+		// GetSunColor()), but it never meets shadeColorFromSun in any expression: it is a SKY-side
+		// quantity that has to keep its weight relative to the Nishita dome, not to the sun. Leaving
+		// out the divide, while the dome took r_SceneReferredNishitaScale, made the haze PI / 0.37 =
+		// 8.5x stronger relative to the sky than stock - a flat grey slab that replaced the sky above
+		// the cloud line, with a hard edge at the volume's lower boundary (research/s9-cloud-haze-
+		// ratio.md, decisions/s9-cloud-haze.md, 2026-09-09). So on the scene-referred path the haze
+		// follows the DOME's convention: the same divide stock applies, and the same Nishita scale
+		// the dome takes in CSkyLightManager::UpdateInternal. Off the switch the stock expression is
+		// evaluated unchanged.
+		float sunIntensityOriginal = (sunIntensityLux / RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE) / gf_PI; // divided by pi to match to GetSunColor(), it's also divided by pi in ConvertIlluminanceToLightColor().
+		if (bSceneReferredUnits)
+		{
+			const ICVar* const pNishitaScale = gEnv->pConsole ? gEnv->pConsole->GetCVar("r_SceneReferredNishitaScale") : nullptr;
+			const float nishitaScale = pNishitaScale ? pNishitaScale->GetFVal() : 1.0f;
+			if (nishitaScale > 0.0f)
+				sunIntensityOriginal *= nishitaScale;
+		}
 		const float sunIntensityCustomSun = cloudShadingMultipliers.x * cloudShadingCustomSunColorMult;
 		const float sunIntensityCloudAtmosphere = Lerp(sunIntensityOriginal, sunIntensityCustomSun, cloudShadingCustomSunColorInfluence);
 		const float atmosphericScatteringMultiplier = GetValue(PARAM_VOLCLOUD_ATMOSPHERIC_SCATTERING).x;
